  "summary": "Reverse shell to ngrok tunnel executed on npm install",
  "details": "package.json declares a postinstall hook that runs poc.js on `npm install`. poc.js requires child_process, opens a TCP socket to 0.tcp.in.ngrok.io:19775, spawns /bin/sh, and pipes the socket to the shell's stdin/stdout/stderr. This yields an unauthenticated reverse shell on the installer's host, executed automatically without user interaction during a normal install.",
